{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794698013,"nonce":"pNamL8/vOkbNeDtNbHmuvlKlRFU=","title":"hxnsl: a Haxe shader language compiled for every GPU target at build time","message":"The goal is shaders written in Haxe that come out of the build as WGSL, MSL,\nHLSL, SPIR-V and GLSL ES, so no Naga or other shader compiler runs in the\nprogram. hxnsl replaces the per-binding copy of HXSL that hlwgpu carries.\n\nShape:\n\n- Front end: a Haxe build macro, lifted from hlwgpu's HXSL: its syntax,\n  checker, linker, stage splitter and dead-code elimination. Errors point at\n  Haxe source. It emits WGSL.\n- Back end: russl_compiler (project-blinc/russl), which writes every target\n  from a Naga module, with a fixed binding model per target that it reports in\n  `reflection.native`. It runs in a small build-time tool, shipped prebuilt in\n  the haxelib for each host, as hlwgpu's hxsl-naga is.\n- Output on each shader class: each target's source, the bind group layout,\n  entry points and native slots.\n\nNeeds from russl: a public entry point that takes WGSL or a Naga module and\nreturns its Artifacts with `reflection.native` filled. The user asked for this\nto be worked out with Blinc's session; the request has been sent.\n\nOpen: russl pins Naga ~26 for Blinc; hlwgpu's wgpu is 30. A driver of hxn's\nown binds by russl's slots and does not care; a backend that goes through\nwgpu's passthrough needs the numbering of the wgpu it runs.\n\nWebGL2 is the browser fallback where WebGPU is missing, through hxn's wasm\npath, so the GLSL ES target matters. A shader that needs what WebGL2 lacks,\nsuch as storage buffers, has no GLSL.\n\nSupersedes hlwgpu's hxsl-naga (hlwgpu f662af2, held unpushed), which does the\nVulkan half of this with its own tool.","files":null}]}